  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(510.6pt, 803.28pt, "S2 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 20.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0f4761"))
  #line-at(72pt, 90.84pt, "Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 125.28pt, "Sample preparation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 150.595pt, "Black phosphorus (BP) is an extremely air sensitive material with bare samples oxidizing in 20 minutes ")
  #line-at(72pt, 163.191pt, "under ambient atmospheric conditions. To prevent oxidation, both monolayer and bulk BP flakes are ")
  #line-at(72pt, 175.788pt, "exfoliated and encapsulated with hexagonal boron nitride (hBN), in a nitrogen-filled glovebox (MBraun ")
  #line-at(72pt, 188.506pt, "Unilab pro sp) with O")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(168.6pt, 189.48pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(172.08pt, 188.52pt, " concentration < 2 ppm and H")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(303.6pt, 189.48pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.96pt, 188.52pt, "O concentration < 1 ppm.  ")
  #line-at(71.996pt, 213.835pt, "We first transfer a thin flake of hBN (~ 50 nm) onto a 0.15 mm thick borosilicate glass substrate (VWR ")
  #line-at(71.985pt, 226.431pt, "VistaVision No. 1.5 Square Cover Glasses). The substrate is then annealed in the glovebox at 500°C to ")
  #line-at(71.985pt, 239.149pt, "remove adsorbed oxygen and water on the hBN surface. ")
  #line-at(71.985pt, 264.343pt, "We then exfoliate BP via standard scotch-tape exfoliation techniques onto a PDMS substrate (3 cm × 3 ")
  #line-at(71.985pt, 277.061pt, "cm) placed on a glass slide. Monolayer BP flakes on the substrate are then located using a home-built ")
  #line-at(71.985pt, 289.657pt, "automated scanning system as follows: The substrate is illuminated by a 470 nm light source and then ")
  #line-at(71.996pt, 302.375pt, "imaged through a 760 ± 10 nm bandpass filter to identify fluorescence of monolayer BP flakes. An ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 314.972pt, "automated system scans through the area of the substrate and locates possible monolayer flakes by this ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 327.569pt, "method. For both monolayer and bulk flakes, the PDMS substrate is then cut around the location of a ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 340.287pt, "selected flake to prepare a stamp of area 5 mm × 5 mm. The flake is then transferred onto the prepared ")
  #line-at(72.007pt, 352.883pt, "substrate of hBN on cover glass and subsequently encapsulated with another layer of hBN to prevent ")
  #line-at(71.996pt, 365.601pt, "degradation. ")
  #line-at(71.996pt, 390.795pt, "A rubber O-ring (inner diameter 1 cm) is then glued onto the substrate, encircling the sample, and ")
  #line-at(72.007pt, 403.513pt, "capped by another square cover glass. This is done to further isolate the sample from ambient air ")
  #line-at(72.007pt, 416.109pt, "conditions during transport and measurements. The sample is measured through the glass on which the ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 428.828pt, "encapsulated BP stack rests (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(199.331pt, 428.828pt, "Figure S1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(244.686pt, 428.828pt, "). ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 454.021pt, "Samples made following this procedure have been characterized by absorption and photoluminescence ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 466.739pt, "measurements. They have shown narrow excitonic features (~ 15 meV) at low temperatures (~ 4 K) ")
  #line-at(72.018pt, 479.336pt, "soon after fabrication")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.2pt, 475.44pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(169.68pt, 479.4pt, ". ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(71.998pt, 504.715pt, "stroboSCAT microscopy ")
